          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: The witness observes an orange ball that he initially mistakes for a planet, but realizes it is moving. He records a video and then sees the object disappear along a vertical trajectory. The observation of an orange ball crossing the sky in just a few minutes, on a weekend night, strongly suggests a Thai lantern, likely released nearby after a private party. Meteociel indicates a light southeast wind consistent with the observed movement: weather. The photos leave no doubt about the nature of the object (P1050985 and especially 86, the others are blurry due to focus or movement). However, the witness rejects this hypothesis. The GEIPAN classifies this case as \"A\": observation of a Thai lantern.",
